- **Verified API facts:**
  - Options: `booleanOption/stringOption/intOption(key, default, values, title, description)` — `values: Map<String,T>`
    renders a preset DROPDOWN (key = machine value, value = display name) → use for device/SIM presets.
    File-scope declare + call `optionName()` inside patch to register; declaring inside the patch body auto-registers.
  - Smali: `replaceInstruction(index, smali)` (1 instruction) · `replaceInstructions(index, "multi-line")` (1→N).
    Inline smali compiles against the method's CURRENT register count → only use registers that already exist
    (move-result dest regs; method-entry inserts may clobber dead local v0 / last param). NEVER grow registerCount.
  - resourcePatch ctx: `document(path)`, `get(path, copy=false)`, `listApkEntries(prefix)`, `delete(path)`.
  - bytecodePatch ctx: `classDefForEach`, `classDefBy`, `mutableClassDefBy`, shared `patchMatchingMethods`.
  - `extensions/extension` (.mpe) module exists but NO patch uses extendWith yet — needed if a fake object must be fabricated.
- **Conventions (all 10 existing patches):** `default = false`; `category(...)`; 3rd-person present-tense description
  ending in a period; `@Suppress("unused")` on the top-level patch val; dual patches = private UNNAMED bytecodePatch +
  `dependsOn` + file-scope options (see AllowScreenshotsPatch.kt / StripTrackersPatch.kt); document ceilings with `ponytail:` comments.
- Shared helpers already written (this effort): `shared/ConstTracking.kt` (argumentRegisters, methodReferenceOf,
